before:
```typescript
interface Captioned {
  caption(): string;
}
class Badge implements Captioned {
  label: string;
  constructor(label: string) { this.label = label; }
  caption(): string { return "Badge: " + this.label; }
}
const badge = new Badge("Helper");
console.log(badge.caption());
```
This prints Badge: Helper. Captioned declares caption():string: no inputs and a text result. new Badge passes a label to the constructor, which stores it. badge.caption() calls the method on that instance; this.label reads its stored label, and return sends the prefixed text back. console.log displays that returned text.

