after:
```typescript
interface Captioned {
  caption(): string;
}
class Badge implements Captioned {
  label: string;
  constructor(label: string) {
    this.label = label;
  }
  caption(): string {
    return "Badge: " + this.label;
  }
}
const badge = new Badge("Helper");
console.log(badge.caption());
```
This prints `Badge: Helper`. `Captioned` requires a `caption` method that returns text. A method is a function that belongs to an object.
